<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Softline buys PC importer for 39 mln rand.</title>
<headline>Softline buys PC importer for 39 mln rand.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>South African information technology firm Softline Ltd, which listed on the Johannesburg Stock Exchange last month, said on Wednesday it had acquired Personal Computer Importers as a going concern for 38.73 million rand.</p>
<p>The purchase will be settled through the issue of 18.1 million new shares at 214 cents each.</p>
<p>The company also said it was negotiating another acquisition.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
